<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proofs</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Conditional carré du champ matching ‣ 3 Conditional metric matching ‣ Riemannian Metric Matchingfor Scalable Geometric Modeling of Distributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z:=\Gamma_{\varepsilon}(f,h)(X,Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z:=\Gamma_{\varepsilon}(f,h)(X,Y)</annotation></semantics></math> be the random variable defined by <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim p</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\mid X\sim\mathcal{N}(X,{\varepsilon}I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\mid X\sim\mathcal{N}(X,{\varepsilon}I)</annotation></semantics></math>, so <a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ 3.1 Conditional carré du champ matching ‣ 3 Conditional metric matching ‣ Riemannian Metric Matchingfor Scalable Geometric Modeling of Distributions" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.​ 9</span></a> says that <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[Z\mid Y]=\Gamma_{\varepsilon}(f,h)(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[Z\mid Y]=\Gamma_{\varepsilon}(f,h)(Y)</annotation></semantics></math>.
We can apply the law of total expectation and bias-variance decomposition to derive</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}^{CDC}_{cond}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}^{CDC}_{cond}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\EX\left[(\Gamma_{\varepsilon}^{\theta}(Y)-Z)^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\EX\left[(\Gamma_{\varepsilon}^{\theta}(Y)-Z)^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\EX\left[\EX\left[(\Gamma_{\varepsilon}^{\theta}(Y)-Z)^{2}\mid Y\right]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\EX\left[\EX\left[(\Gamma_{\varepsilon}^{\theta}(Y)-Z)^{2}\mid Y\right]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\EX\left[\left(\Gamma_{\varepsilon}^{\theta}(Y)-\mathbb{E}[Z\mid Y]\right)^{2}+\operatorname{Var}(Z\mid Y)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\EX\left[\left(\Gamma_{\varepsilon}^{\theta}(Y)-\mathbb{E}[Z\mid Y]\right)^{2}+\operatorname{Var}(Z\mid Y)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\EX\left[\left(\Gamma_{\varepsilon}^{\theta}(Y)-\Gamma_{\varepsilon}(f,h)(Y)\right)^{2}\right]+\EX\left[\operatorname{Var}(Z\mid Y)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\EX\left[\left(\Gamma_{\varepsilon}^{\theta}(Y)-\Gamma_{\varepsilon}(f,h)(Y)\right)^{2}\right]+\EX\left[\operatorname{Var}(Z\mid Y)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{L}^{CDC}_{marg}(\theta)+\EX\left[\operatorname{Var}(Z\mid Y)\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{L}^{CDC}_{marg}(\theta)+\EX\left[\operatorname{Var}(Z\mid Y)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">so the result holds with <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=\EX\left[\operatorname{Var}(Z\mid Y)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=\EX\left[\operatorname{Var}(Z\mid Y)\right]</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1 (Convergence of the carré du champ). ‣ 4.1 Recovering the metric from an embedded manifold ‣ 4 Convergence and the Riemannian toolkit ‣ Riemannian Metric Matchingfor Scalable Geometric Modeling of Distributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We would first like to show that, by possibly reducing <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> to any <math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\delta^{\prime}&lt;\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\delta^{\prime}&lt;\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, we can assume that <math id="A1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}=B(x,\delta)\cap\text{supp}(\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}=B(x,\delta)\cap\text{supp}(\mu)</annotation></semantics></math> is a compact manifold with boundary.
By assumption, <math id="A1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> is a smooth manifold of <math id="A1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, so the ambient distance function <math id="A1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\mapsto\|y-x\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\mapsto\|y-x\|</annotation></semantics></math> restricts to a smooth function <math id="A1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{x}:\mathcal{M}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{x}:\mathcal{M}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In particular, <math id="A1.p4.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{M}=d_{x}^{-1}[0,\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}=d_{x}^{-1}[0,\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}^{\prime}=d_{x}^{-1}[0,\delta^{\prime}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}^{\prime}=d_{x}^{-1}[0,\delta^{\prime}]</annotation></semantics></math> is a compact submanifold of <math id="A1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> with boundary (that is also a submanifold of <math id="A1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>), and satisfies all the other conditions on <math id="A1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We can now apply the </span><span id="A1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">diffusion maps</span><span id="A1.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text"> theorem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Coifman and Lafon, 2006</a>; <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Belkin and Niyogi, 2003</a>)</cite> to the operator <math id="A1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\epsilon}:=({\mathbf{I}}-P_{\varepsilon})/{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\epsilon}:=({\mathbf{I}}-P_{\varepsilon})/{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let us write <math id="A1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> for the induced Riemannian metric on <math id="A1.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> for its Laplace-Beltrami operator, and <math id="A1.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> for the smooth density of <math id="A1.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to the Riemannian volume form of <math id="A1.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{M},g)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{M},g)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, for smooth <math id="A1.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>, Theorem 2 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Coifman and Lafon, 2006</a>)</cite> (applied here with <math id="A1.p4.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0</annotation></semantics></math>) states that
<math id="A1.p4.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{L}_{\epsilon}f-\mathcal{L}f|\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{L}_{\epsilon}f-\mathcal{L}f|\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>
as <math id="A1.p4.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, where</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}f=\frac{\Delta_{g}(fp)-\Delta_{g}(p)f}{p}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}f=\frac{\Delta_{g}(fp)-\Delta_{g}(p)f}{p}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">We can apply the carré du champ identity <a href="#S2.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ Diffusion geometry and the carré du champ. ‣ 2 Background ‣ Riemannian Metric Matchingfor Scalable Geometric Modeling of Distributions" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.​ 2</span></a> to write</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{g}(fp)-\Delta_{g}(p)f=\Delta_{g}(f)p-2g(\nabla p,\nabla f)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{g}(fp)-\Delta_{g}(p)f=\Delta_{g}(f)p-2g(\nabla p,\nabla f),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">so</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}f=\Delta_{g}f-2\frac{g(\nabla p,\nabla f)}{p}=\Delta_{g}f-2g(\nabla\log p,\nabla f)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}f=\Delta_{g}f-2\frac{g(\nabla p,\nabla f)}{p}=\Delta_{g}f-2g(\nabla\log p,\nabla f).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">We can now again use the carré du champ identity to expand</span></p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Gamma_{\varepsilon}(f,g)-g_{x}(\nabla f,\nabla h)|=\frac{1}{2}\big|f(\mathcal{L}_{\varepsilon}h-\Delta_{g}h)+h(\mathcal{L}_{\varepsilon}f-\Delta_{g}f)-(\mathcal{L}_{\varepsilon}(fh)-\Delta_{g}(fh))\big|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Gamma_{\varepsilon}(f,g)-g_{x}(\nabla f,\nabla h)|=\frac{1}{2}\big|f(\mathcal{L}_{\varepsilon}h-\Delta_{g}h)+h(\mathcal{L}_{\varepsilon}f-\Delta_{g}f)-(\mathcal{L}_{\varepsilon}(fh)-\Delta_{g}(fh))\big|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">and notice that each term satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\varepsilon}h-\Delta_{g}h=\mathcal{L}_{\varepsilon}h-\mathcal{L}h+\mathcal{L}h-\Delta_{g}h=(\mathcal{L}_{\varepsilon}h-\mathcal{L}h)-2g(\nabla\log p,\nabla h)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\varepsilon}h-\Delta_{g}h=\mathcal{L}_{\varepsilon}h-\mathcal{L}h+\mathcal{L}h-\Delta_{g}h=(\mathcal{L}_{\varepsilon}h-\mathcal{L}h)-2g(\nabla\log p,\nabla h),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">so <a href="#A1.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Riemannian Metric Matchingfor Scalable Geometric Modeling of Distributions" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.​ 17</span></a> becomes</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}\big|f[\mathcal{L}_{\varepsilon}h-\mathcal{L}h]+h[\mathcal{L}_{\varepsilon}f-\mathcal{L}f]-[\mathcal{L}_{\varepsilon}(fh)-\mathcal{L}(fh)]-2fg(\nabla\log p,\nabla h)-2hg(\nabla\log p,\nabla f)+2g(\nabla\log p,\nabla(fh))\big|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}\big|f[\mathcal{L}_{\varepsilon}h-\mathcal{L}h]+h[\mathcal{L}_{\varepsilon}f-\mathcal{L}f]-[\mathcal{L}_{\varepsilon}(fh)-\mathcal{L}(fh)]-2fg(\nabla\log p,\nabla h)-2hg(\nabla\log p,\nabla f)+2g(\nabla\log p,\nabla(fh))\big|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.7.1" class="ltx_text">We can apply the Leibniz rule to</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-2fg(\nabla\log p,\nabla h)-2hg(\nabla\log p,\nabla f)+2g(\nabla\log p,\nabla(fh))=2g(\nabla\log p,\nabla(fh)-f\nabla h-h\nabla f)=0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>f</mi><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-2fg(\nabla\log p,\nabla h)-2hg(\nabla\log p,\nabla f)+2g(\nabla\log p,\nabla(fh))=2g(\nabla\log p,\nabla(fh)-f\nabla h-h\nabla f)=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.8.1" class="ltx_text">and so find that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Gamma_{\varepsilon}(f,g)-g_{x}(\nabla f,\nabla h)|\leq\frac{1}{2}\big(|f||\mathcal{L}_{\varepsilon}h-\mathcal{L}h|+|h||\mathcal{L}_{\varepsilon}f-\mathcal{L}f|+|\mathcal{L}_{\varepsilon}(fh)-\mathcal{L}(fh)|\big)\to 0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Gamma_{\varepsilon}(f,g)-g_{x}(\nabla f,\nabla h)|\leq\frac{1}{2}\big(|f||\mathcal{L}_{\varepsilon}h-\mathcal{L}h|+|h||\mathcal{L}_{\varepsilon}f-\mathcal{L}f|+|\mathcal{L}_{\varepsilon}(fh)-\mathcal{L}(fh)|\big)\to 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.9.1" class="ltx_text">as <math id="A1.p4.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="A1.p4.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{L}_{\epsilon}f-\mathcal{L}f|\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{L}_{\epsilon}f-\mathcal{L}f|\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p4.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f,h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f,h</annotation></semantics></math> are bounded (which is implied by the fact that <math id="A1.p4.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> is compact).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Existence of a low-rank factorization if <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=2d-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=2d-1</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G({\mathbf{p}})=(\Gamma(x_{i},x_{j})({\mathbf{p}}))_{i,j=1,...,D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G({\mathbf{p}})=(\Gamma(x_{i},x_{j})({\mathbf{p}}))_{i,j=1,...,D}</annotation></semantics></math> be the <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\times D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\times D</annotation></semantics></math> carré du champ matrix of the ambient coordinates at <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐩</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{p}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, for <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=2d-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=2d-1</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\times D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\times D</annotation></semantics></math> matrix <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M({\mathbf{p}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M({\mathbf{p}})</annotation></semantics></math>, whose entries are all smooth functions, such that <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G({\mathbf{p}})=M({\mathbf{p}})^{T}M({\mathbf{p}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G({\mathbf{p}})=M({\mathbf{p}})^{T}M({\mathbf{p}})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{p}}\in\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{p}}\in\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> be a smooth <math id="A1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional manifold.
If <math id="A1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the tangent bundle is trivial,
so the result follows directly with <math id="A1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="A1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, Whitney’s immersion theorem gives a smooth immersion
<math id="A1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:\mathcal{M}\to\mathbb{R}^{2d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:\mathcal{M}\to\mathbb{R}^{2d-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By definition, this means that the differential <math id="A1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\phi:T\mathcal{M}\to T\mathbb{R}^{K}\cong\mathbb{R}^{K}\times\mathbb{R}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\phi:T\mathcal{M}\to T\mathbb{R}^{K}\cong\mathbb{R}^{K}\times\mathbb{R}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> defines an injective map <math id="A1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\phi_{p}:T_{p}\mathcal{M}\to\mathbb{R}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\phi_{p}:T_{p}\mathcal{M}\to\mathbb{R}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{p}}\in\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{p}}\in\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In other words, <math id="A1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\phi</annotation></semantics></math> is a smooth embedding of vector bundles <math id="A1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\mathcal{M}\to{\varepsilon}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\mathcal{M}\to{\varepsilon}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>K</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is the trivial bundle of rank <math id="A1.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>.
We would like this derivative to be an isometry on each tangent space, i.e. that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{p}(u,v)=\langle d\phi_{p}(u),d\phi_{p}(v)\rangle_{\mathbb{R}^{K}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{p}(u,v)=\langle d\phi_{p}(u),d\phi_{p}(v)\rangle_{\mathbb{R}^{K}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">for all <math id="A1.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,v\in T_{p}\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,v\in T_{p}\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, and we will now construct a smooth bundle map <math id="A1.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi:T\mathcal{M}\to{\varepsilon}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi:T\mathcal{M}\to{\varepsilon}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> that satisfies this.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let us define a new Riemannian metric <math id="A1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\mathbf{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>𝐩</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\mathbf{p}}</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{p}(u,v)=\langle d\phi_{p}(u),d\phi_{p}(v)\rangle_{\mathbb{R}^{K}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{p}(u,v)=\langle d\phi_{p}(u),d\phi_{p}(v)\rangle_{\mathbb{R}^{K}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">for <math id="A1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,v\in T_{p}\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,v\in T_{p}\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is strictly positive definite because <math id="A1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\phi</annotation></semantics></math> is injective.
Since <math id="A1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> is smooth and <math id="A1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\phi</annotation></semantics></math> is injective for all <math id="A1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐩</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{p}}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a unique smooth section of the bundle of symmetric endomorphisms, <math id="A1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\Gamma(\text{End}(T\mathcal{M}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>End</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\Gamma(\text{End}(T\mathcal{M}))</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{p}(A_{p}u,v)=h_{p}(u,v)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{p}(A_{p}u,v)=h_{p}(u,v)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">for all <math id="A1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,v\in T_{p}\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,v\in T_{p}\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, which we can think of as the matrix representation of the quadratic form <math id="A1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\mathbf{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>𝐩</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\mathbf{p}}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to the inner product <math id="A1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\mathbf{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝐩</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\mathbf{p}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Both <math id="A1.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> are positive-definite inner products, so the operator <math id="A1.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> must be symmetric and positive-definite with respect to <math id="A1.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in M</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">We would now like to compute the inverse square root <math id="A1.p7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A^{-1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{-1/2}</annotation></semantics></math> as another smooth section in <math id="A1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma(\text{End}(T\mathcal{M}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>End</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma(\text{End}(T\mathcal{M}))</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> is positive-definite, its eigenvalues are strictly positive real numbers.
The function <math id="A1.p7.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f(x)=x^{-1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)=x^{-1/2}</annotation></semantics></math> is smooth on the interval <math id="A1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math> and so, by the spectral theorem and standard functional calculus, the operator field <math id="A1.p7.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A^{-1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{-1/2}</annotation></semantics></math> is a well-defined, smooth section of <math id="A1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{End}(T\mathcal{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>End</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{End}(T\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now define a new bundle map <math id="A1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi:T\mathcal{M}\to\mathbb{R}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi:T\mathcal{M}\to\mathbb{R}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> by pre-composing the immersion differential with the correction operator</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Psi_{p}:=d\phi_{p}\circ A_{p}^{-1/2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{p}:=d\phi_{p}\circ A_{p}^{-1/2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">which is an isometry since</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle\Psi_{p}u,\Psi_{p}v\rangle_{\mathbb{R}^{K}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle\Psi_{p}u,\Psi_{p}v\rangle_{\mathbb{R}^{K}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex31.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\langle d\phi_{p}(A_{p}^{-1/2}u),d\phi_{p}(A_{p}^{-1/2}v)\rangle_{\mathbb{R}^{K}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\langle d\phi_{p}(A_{p}^{-1/2}u),d\phi_{p}(A_{p}^{-1/2}v)\rangle_{\mathbb{R}^{K}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=h_{p}(A_{p}^{-1/2}u,A_{p}^{-1/2}v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=h_{p}(A_{p}^{-1/2}u,A_{p}^{-1/2}v)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=g_{p}(A_{p}(A_{p}^{-1/2}u),A_{p}^{-1/2}v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=g_{p}(A_{p}(A_{p}^{-1/2}u),A_{p}^{-1/2}v)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=g_{p}(A_{p}^{-1/2}A_{p}A_{p}^{-1/2}u,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=g_{p}(A_{p}^{-1/2}A_{p}A_{p}^{-1/2}u,v)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=g_{p}(u,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=g_{p}(u,v)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">for all <math id="A1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,v\in T_{p}\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,v\in T_{p}\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We can now construct the matrix <math id="A1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\times D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\times D</annotation></semantics></math> factor <math id="A1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M({\mathbf{p}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M({\mathbf{p}})</annotation></semantics></math> using the <math id="A1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> components of this bundle map.
If <math id="A1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{1},\dots,e_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{1},\dots,e_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> are the standard basis of <math id="A1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},\dots,x_{D}:\mathcal{M}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},\dots,x_{D}:\mathcal{M}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> are the ambient coordinate functions of <math id="A1.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A1.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, then we can set</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{ij}=\langle e_{i},\Psi(\nabla x_{j})\rangle_{\mathbb{R}^{K}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{ij}=\langle e_{i},\Psi(\nabla x_{j})\rangle_{\mathbb{R}^{K}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">which are all smooth functions, and find that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(M^{T}M)_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(M^{T}M)_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{r=1}^{K}M_{ri}M_{rj}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{r=1}^{K}M_{ri}M_{rj}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{r=1}^{K}\langle e_{r},\Psi(\nabla x_{i})\rangle\langle e_{r},\Psi(\nabla x_{j})\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{r=1}^{K}\langle e_{r},\Psi(\nabla x_{i})\rangle\langle e_{r},\Psi(\nabla x_{j})\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\langle\Psi(\nabla x_{i}),\Psi(\nabla x_{j})\rangle_{\mathbb{R}^{K}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\langle\Psi(\nabla x_{i}),\Psi(\nabla x_{j})\rangle_{\mathbb{R}^{K}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=g(\nabla x_{i},\nabla x_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=g(\nabla x_{i},\nabla x_{j})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">for each <math id="A1.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j=1,...,D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j=1,...,D</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">The Lemma demonstrates that the low-rank loss and the metric matching loss have the same minimzer for <math id="A1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq 2d-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq 2d-1</annotation></semantics></math>, and so we immediately attain the following theorem as a consequence.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4.4 (Low-rank training is valid for 𝑟≥2⁢𝑑-1). ‣ 4.2 Low-rank training is valid for 𝑟≥2⁢𝑑-1 ‣ 4 Convergence and the Riemannian toolkit ‣ Riemannian Metric Matchingfor Scalable Geometric Modeling of Distributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Extended comparison to higher order score matching.</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We relate our conditional CDC objective to higher-order score matching <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Meng et al., 2021</a>)</cite>, that propose a method to learn the higher order scores <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{k}(x)=\nabla^{k}\log p_{\varepsilon}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{k}(x)=\nabla^{k}\log p_{\varepsilon}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> for order <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\varepsilon}=p_{\text{data}}\star\mathcal{N}(0,{\varepsilon}I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋆</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\varepsilon}=p_{\text{data}}\star\mathcal{N}(0,{\varepsilon}I)</annotation></semantics></math>. In the second order case they parameterize a first-order score network <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{1}^{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1}^{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and a second-order network <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{2}^{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{2}^{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, trained jointly via score matching and a second-order regression loss of the form</p>
<table id="A2.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{X,Y|X}\Big\|s_{2}^{\theta}(Y)+s_{1}^{\theta}(Y)s_{1}^{\theta}(Y)^{\top}+\frac{I-\frac{1}{{\varepsilon}}(X-Y)(X-Y)^{\top}}{{\varepsilon}}\Big\|_{F}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{X,Y|X}\Big\|s_{2}^{\theta}(Y)+s_{1}^{\theta}(Y)s_{1}^{\theta}(Y)^{\top}+\frac{I-\frac{1}{{\varepsilon}}(X-Y)(X-Y)^{\top}}{{\varepsilon}}\Big\|_{F}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(y):=s_{2}(y)+s_{1}(y)s_{1}(y)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(y):=s_{2}(y)+s_{1}(y)s_{1}(y)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>. Optimizing the above yields the conditional identity</p>
<table id="A2.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(y)=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\frac{I-\frac{1}{{\varepsilon}}(X-Y)(X-Y)^{\top}}{{\varepsilon}}\,\middle|\,Y=y\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mi>ε</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(y)=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\frac{I-\frac{1}{{\varepsilon}}(X-Y)(X-Y)^{\top}}{{\varepsilon}}\,\middle|\,Y=y\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">With our definition <math id="A2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma^{*}(y):=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\frac{(X-Y)(X-Y)^{\top}}{2{\varepsilon}}\,\middle|\,Y=y\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma^{*}(y):=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\frac{(X-Y)(X-Y)^{\top}}{2{\varepsilon}}\,\middle|\,Y=y\right],</annotation></semantics></math> we obtain the exact relationship <math id="A2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}A^{*}(y)\;=\;I-2\Gamma^{*}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}A^{*}(y)\;=\;I-2\Gamma^{*}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>. While <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Meng et al. (2021)</a></cite> do not discuss convergence as <math id="A2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> under manifold-supported data, we observe that <math id="A2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma^{*}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma^{*}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> remains bounded and converges to the tangent-space projector, while <math id="A2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> (and hence <math id="A2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>) typically contains <math id="A2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(1/{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(1/{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> components in directions normal to the manifold and can therefore diverge as <math id="A2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Additionally, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Meng et al., 2021</a>)</cite> do not use the low-rank loss decomposition discussed in <a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4 Positive semi-definite and low rank training ‣ 3 Conditional metric matching ‣ Riemannian Metric Matchingfor Scalable Geometric Modeling of Distributions" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.​ 3.4</span></a> which reduces the loss’ complexity from <math id="A2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(D^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(D^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(D)</annotation></semantics></math>, which is crucial to applying the loss to high dimensional images. Recently, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kharitenko et al. (2025)</a></cite> showed that <math id="A2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{I}}-{\varepsilon}s_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{I}}-{\varepsilon}s_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> converges to the projection on the tangent space of the manifold as <math id="A2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that this is consistent with our results: <math id="A2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}A^{*}={\varepsilon}s_{2}+{\varepsilon}s_{1}s_{1}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}A^{*}={\varepsilon}s_{2}+{\varepsilon}s_{1}s_{1}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="A2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}s_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}s_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> term dies because <math id="A2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> remains bounded on the manifold, leaving only the <math id="A2.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}s_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}s_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> term, and both converge to the same object.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Low rank loss derivation</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When the metric is parameterized as low rank with small identity perturbation <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}={M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}+\lambda\mathbf{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}={M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}+\lambda\mathbf{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=Y-X\sim\mathcal{N}(0,{\varepsilon}{\mathbf{I}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=Y-X\sim\mathcal{N}(0,{\varepsilon}{\mathbf{I}})</annotation></semantics></math> be the noise, then:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|{M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}+\lambda\mathbf{I}-\frac{1}{2{\varepsilon}}\Delta\Delta^{T}\right\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|{M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}+\lambda\mathbf{I}-\frac{1}{2{\varepsilon}}\Delta\Delta^{T}\right\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Tr\left(\left({M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}+\lambda\mathbf{I}-\frac{1}{2{\varepsilon}}\Delta\Delta^{T}\right)^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Tr\left(\left({M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}+\lambda\mathbf{I}-\frac{1}{2{\varepsilon}}\Delta\Delta^{T}\right)^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Tr\left(\left({M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}+\lambda{\mathbf{I}}\right)^{2}+\left(\frac{1}{2{\varepsilon}}\Delta\Delta^{T}\right)^{2}-\frac{1}{{\varepsilon}}\left({M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}+\lambda{\mathbf{I}}\right)\Delta\Delta^{T}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Tr\left(\left({M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}+\lambda{\mathbf{I}}\right)^{2}+\left(\frac{1}{2{\varepsilon}}\Delta\Delta^{T}\right)^{2}-\frac{1}{{\varepsilon}}\left({M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}+\lambda{\mathbf{I}}\right)\Delta\Delta^{T}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Tr\left(\left({M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\right)^{2}\right)+2\lambda\Tr\left({M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\right)+\lambda^{2}D+\Tr\left(\left(\frac{1}{2{\varepsilon}}\Delta\Delta^{T}\right)^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Tr\left(\left({M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\right)^{2}\right)+2\lambda\Tr\left({M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\right)+\lambda^{2}D+\Tr\left(\left(\frac{1}{2{\varepsilon}}\Delta\Delta^{T}\right)^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ \ -\frac{1}{{\varepsilon}}\left(\Tr\left({M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\Delta\Delta^{T}\right)+\lambda\Tr\left(\Delta\Delta^{T}\right)\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ \ -\frac{1}{{\varepsilon}}\left(\Tr\left({M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\Delta\Delta^{T}\right)+\lambda\Tr\left(\Delta\Delta^{T}\right)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Where we expanded the squares. Now we notice that <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Tr\left((\Delta\Delta^{T})^{2}\right)=\Tr\left(\Delta\Delta^{T}\Delta\Delta^{T}\right)=\|\Delta\|_{2}^{2}\Tr\left(\Delta\Delta^{T}\right)=\|\Delta\|_{2}^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Tr\left((\Delta\Delta^{T})^{2}\right)=\Tr\left(\Delta\Delta^{T}\Delta\Delta^{T}\right)=\|\Delta\|_{2}^{2}\Tr\left(\Delta\Delta^{T}\right)=\|\Delta\|_{2}^{4}</annotation></semantics></math>, and due to the cyclic property of the trace (i.e. <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Tr(ABC)=\Tr(CAB)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Tr(ABC)=\Tr(CAB)</annotation></semantics></math>), we have <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Tr\left({M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\Delta\Delta^{T}\right)=\Tr\left(\Delta^{T}{M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\Delta\right)=\Tr\left(\left(M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\Delta\right)^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\Delta\right)=\|M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\Delta\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Tr\left({M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\Delta\Delta^{T}\right)=\Tr\left(\Delta^{T}{M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\Delta\right)=\Tr\left(\left(M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\Delta\right)^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\Delta\right)=\|M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\Delta\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Reorganizing the terms we get:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|{M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}+\lambda\mathbf{I}-\frac{1}{2{\varepsilon}}\Delta\Delta^{T}\right\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|{M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}+\lambda\mathbf{I}-\frac{1}{2{\varepsilon}}\Delta\Delta^{T}\right\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Tr\left(\left({M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\right)^{2}\right)+2\lambda\Tr\left({M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\right)-\frac{1}{{\varepsilon}}\|M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\Delta\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Tr\left(\left({M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\right)^{2}\right)+2\lambda\Tr\left({M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\right)-\frac{1}{{\varepsilon}}\|M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\Delta\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ \ \ \ +\underbrace{\lambda^{2}D+\frac{1}{4{\varepsilon}^{2}}\|\Delta\|_{2}^{4}-\frac{\lambda}{{\varepsilon}}\|\Delta\|_{2}^{2}}_{\text{independent of }\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>independent of </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ \ \ \ +\underbrace{\lambda^{2}D+\frac{1}{4{\varepsilon}^{2}}\|\Delta\|_{2}^{4}-\frac{\lambda}{{\varepsilon}}\|\Delta\|_{2}^{2}}_{\text{independent of }\theta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\|{M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\|_{F}^{2}+2\lambda\|M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\|^{2}_{F}-\frac{1}{{\varepsilon}}\|M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\Delta\|_{2}^{2}+C." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\|{M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\|_{F}^{2}+2\lambda\|M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\|^{2}_{F}-\frac{1}{{\varepsilon}}\|M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\Delta\|_{2}^{2}+C.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Hence we get the low rank with Tikhonov regularization loss <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{LR}^{\lambda}=\|{M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\|_{F}^{2}+2\lambda\|M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\|^{2}_{F}-\frac{1}{{\varepsilon}}\|M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\Delta\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mi>λ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{LR}^{\lambda}=\|{M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\|_{F}^{2}+2\lambda\|M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\|^{2}_{F}-\frac{1}{{\varepsilon}}\|M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\Delta\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and setting <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0</annotation></semantics></math> yields the low rank loss <math id="A3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{LR}=\|{M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\|_{F}^{2}-\frac{1}{{\varepsilon}}\|M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\Delta\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{LR}=\|{M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\|_{F}^{2}-\frac{1}{{\varepsilon}}\|M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\Delta\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that since <math id="A3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\|_{F}^{2}=\Tr\left({M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}{M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\right)=\Tr\left(\left(M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}{M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}\right)\left(M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}{M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\|_{F}^{2}=\Tr\left({M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}{M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}\right)=\Tr\left(\left(M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}{M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}\right)\left(M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}{M^{\theta}_{\varepsilon}}^{T}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|M_{\varepsilon}^{\theta}\|_{F}^{2}=\Tr\left(M_{\varepsilon}^{\theta}{M_{\varepsilon}^{\theta}}^{T}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|M_{\varepsilon}^{\theta}\|_{F}^{2}=\Tr\left(M_{\varepsilon}^{\theta}{M_{\varepsilon}^{\theta}}^{T}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, both terms can be computed without ever materializing any <math id="A3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\times D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\times D</annotation></semantics></math> matrices.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Training Algorithms</h2>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Minibatch training with per-sample noise for Conditional CDC Matching (scalar)</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l0.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0:</span></span>
            
            
           Dataset <math id="alg1.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\{x_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}\subset\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\{x_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}\subset\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>; batch size <math id="alg1.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>; noise-scale sampler <math id="alg1.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p({\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p({\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math>; fixed <math id="alg1.l0.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f,h:\mathbb{R}^{D}\!\to\!\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f,h:\mathbb{R}^{D}\!\to\!\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>; network <math id="alg1.l0.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma^{\theta}:\mathbb{R}^{D}\times\mathbb{R}_{+}\!\to\!\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma^{\theta}:\mathbb{R}^{D}\times\mathbb{R}_{+}\!\to\!\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>; optimizer Opt.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each training step <span id="alg1.l1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
            
            
            Sample minibatch <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=\{X_{b}\}_{b=1}^{B}\sim\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=\{X_{b}\}_{b=1}^{B}\sim\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
            
            
            For each <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>: sample <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}_{b}\sim p({\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}_{b}\sim p({\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
            
            
            For each <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>: sample <math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{b}\sim\mathcal{N}(X_{b},{\varepsilon}_{b}{\mathbf{I}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{b}\sim\mathcal{N}(X_{b},{\varepsilon}_{b}{\mathbf{I}})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
            
            
            Compute <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{b}\leftarrow\big(f(X_{b})-f(Y_{b})\big)\big(h(X_{b})-h(Y_{b})\big)/2{\varepsilon}_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{b}\leftarrow\big(f(X_{b})-f(Y_{b})\big)\big(h(X_{b})-h(Y_{b})\big)/2{\varepsilon}_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l5.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;">// conditional CDC target
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
            
            
            Predict <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{b}\leftarrow\Gamma^{\theta}(Y_{b},{\varepsilon}_{b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{b}\leftarrow\Gamma^{\theta}(Y_{b},{\varepsilon}_{b})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
            
            
            Loss <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}\leftarrow\frac{1}{B}\sum_{b=1}^{B}(P_{b}-T_{b})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}\leftarrow\frac{1}{B}\sum_{b=1}^{B}(P_{b}-T_{b})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
            
            
            Update <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\leftarrow\mathrm{Opt}(\theta,\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>Opt</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\leftarrow\mathrm{Opt}(\theta,\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Minibatch training with per-sample noise for Conditional Riemannian Metric Matching (matrix)</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l0.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0:</span></span>
            
            
           Dataset <math id="alg2.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\{x_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}\subset\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\{x_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}\subset\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>; batch size <math id="alg2.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>; noise-scale sampler <math id="alg2.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p({\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p({\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math>; network <math id="alg2.l0.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma^{\theta}:\mathbb{R}^{D}\times\mathbb{R}_{+}\!\to\!\mathbb{S}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma^{\theta}:\mathbb{R}^{D}\times\mathbb{R}_{+}\!\to\!\mathbb{S}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> (predicts symmetric <math id="alg2.l0.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D{\times}D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D{\times}D</annotation></semantics></math>); optimizer Opt.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg2.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each training step <span id="alg2.l1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
            
            
            Sample minibatch <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=\{X_{b}\}_{b=1}^{B}\sim\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=\{X_{b}\}_{b=1}^{B}\sim\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
            
            
            For each <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>: sample <math id="alg2.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}_{b}\sim p({\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}_{b}\sim p({\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> .

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
            
            
            For each <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>: sample <math id="alg2.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{b}\sim\mathcal{N}(X_{b},{\varepsilon}_{b}{\mathbf{I}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{b}\sim\mathcal{N}(X_{b},{\varepsilon}_{b}{\mathbf{I}})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
            
            
            Set <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{b}\leftarrow X_{b}-Y_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{b}\leftarrow X_{b}-Y_{b}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
            
            
            Target <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{b}\leftarrow(\Delta_{b}\Delta_{b}^{\top})/2{\varepsilon}_{b}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{b}\leftarrow(\Delta_{b}\Delta_{b}^{\top})/2{\varepsilon}_{b}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l6.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;">// conditional metric target
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
            
            
            Predict <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{b}\leftarrow\Gamma^{\theta}(Y_{b},{\varepsilon}_{b})\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{b}\leftarrow\Gamma^{\theta}(Y_{b},{\varepsilon}_{b})\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
            
            
            Loss <math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}\leftarrow\frac{1}{B}\sum_{b=1}^{B}\|P_{b}-T_{b}\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}\leftarrow\frac{1}{B}\sum_{b=1}^{B}\|P_{b}-T_{b}\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
            
            
            Update <math id="alg2.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\leftarrow\mathrm{Opt}(\theta,\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>Opt</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\leftarrow\mathrm{Opt}(\theta,\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg2.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Experimental details</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Bandwidth sampling</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In practice we exprimented with two different noise/bandwidth <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> sampling strategies, namely the uniform noise sampling, and log-normal distribution, following the noise scheduling strategy of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Karras et al. (2022)</a></cite>. Specifically, for the log-normal strategy we draw <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log{\varepsilon}\sim\mathcal{N}(P_{\mathrm{mean}},P_{\mathrm{std}}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>mean</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>std</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log{\varepsilon}\sim\mathcal{N}(P_{\mathrm{mean}},P_{\mathrm{std}}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\mathrm{mean}}=-1.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>mean</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1.2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathrm{mean}}=-1.2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\mathrm{std}}=1.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>std</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathrm{std}}=1.2</annotation></semantics></math>, and clamp the resulting values to the interval <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[{\varepsilon}_{\min},{\varepsilon}_{\max}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[{\varepsilon}_{\min},{\varepsilon}_{\max}]</annotation></semantics></math>.
This choice biases sampling toward smaller bandwidths, which are critical for resolving fine-scale geometric structure.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Noise level encoding</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To condition the network on the bandwidth/noise scale <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, we use Fourier feature embeddings of <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> of the form
<math id="A5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{\omega}({\varepsilon})=(\cos({\varepsilon}\omega),\sin({\varepsilon}\omega))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{\omega}({\varepsilon})=(\cos({\varepsilon}\omega),\sin({\varepsilon}\omega))</annotation></semantics></math>.
We use <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d/2</annotation></semantics></math> frequencies given by
<math id="A5.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{k}=T_{\max}^{-\frac{k}{d/2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>max</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{k}=T_{\max}^{-\frac{k}{d/2}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0,\dots,\frac{d}{2}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0,\dots,\frac{d}{2}-1</annotation></semantics></math>,
following standard practice in diffusion and flow-matching models.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.3 </span>Synthetic spheres experiment</h3>

<section id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">FiLM-conditioned residual MLP encoder.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the synthetic sphere experiments, we parameterize the low-rank factor
<math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\theta}_{{\varepsilon}}({\mathbf{y}})\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\theta}_{{\varepsilon}}({\mathbf{y}})\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> with a FiLM-conditioned residual MLP <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Perez et al., 2018</a>)</cite>,
denoted <span id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">MLPEncoder</span>. The network takes as input a point <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> and a per-sample noise/bandwidth scalar <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, and outputs</p>
<table id="A5.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{MLPEncoder}(h,x)\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times D}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">MLPEncoder</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{MLPEncoder}(h,x)\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times D}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This output is used in the low-rank CDC parameterization
<math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma^{\theta}_{{\varepsilon}}({\mathbf{y}})=M^{\theta}_{{\varepsilon}}({\mathbf{y}})^{\top}M^{\theta}_{{\varepsilon}}({\mathbf{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma^{\theta}_{{\varepsilon}}({\mathbf{y}})=M^{\theta}_{{\varepsilon}}({\mathbf{y}})^{\top}M^{\theta}_{{\varepsilon}}({\mathbf{y}})</annotation></semantics></math> (or
equivalently in the low-rank loss that avoids materializing <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma^{\theta}_{{\varepsilon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma^{\theta}_{{\varepsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Output bias.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Optionally, we add an output bias <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{\mathrm{out}}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{\mathrm{out}}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{{\varepsilon}}^{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{{\varepsilon}}^{\theta}({\mathbf{y}})</annotation></semantics></math> before making <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{{\varepsilon}}^{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{{\varepsilon}}^{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, which we find help during early training.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Noise-scale conditioning.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We condition the network on <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> using a sinusoidal noise-level embedding as describe in <a href="#A5.SS2" title="E.2 Noise level encoding ‣ Appendix E Experimental details ‣ Riemannian Metric Matchingfor Scalable Geometric Modeling of Distributions" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.​ E.2</span></a> followed by a small MLP. Concretely, we compute feed the noise-level encoding in a 2-layer MLP with SiLU nonlinearity. This embedding is injected into <em id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">every</em> residual block via FiLM (feature-wise linear modulation) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Perez et al., 2018</a>)</cite>, rather than concatenated only once at the input.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Initialization.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We initialize each residual block near the identity map, meaning a zero initialization of the projection heads of each blocks. Importantly, we do
<em id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not</em> zero-initialize the final projection head: <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math> is initialized
from a zero-mean Gaussian with small standard deviation, and <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{\mathrm{out}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{\mathrm{out}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
This avoids an initial output <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\theta}_{{\varepsilon}}({\mathbf{y}})\approx 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\theta}_{{\varepsilon}}({\mathbf{y}})\approx 0</annotation></semantics></math>, which can lead to weak
gradients when optimizing losses involving <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\top}M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\top}M</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Synthetic sphere configuration.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unless otherwise specified, we use ambient dimension <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=64</annotation></semantics></math> and sphere dimension <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=8</annotation></semantics></math>. The architecture used hidden width <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=1024</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=4</annotation></semantics></math> residual blocks,
rank <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=16</annotation></semantics></math>, and time/noise embedding enabled. We train with AdamW (learning rate
<math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>, no weight decay) for <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3000</annotation></semantics></math> epochs with batch size <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1024</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1024</annotation></semantics></math> and gradient clipping with norm <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.
In this configuration the MLP has roughly <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>15</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">15</annotation></semantics></math>M parameters. The noise level sampling strategy used during training was log-normal with <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\min}=10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\min}=10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\max}=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\max}=16</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation and hyper-parameter tuning for <a href="#S4.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 4.4 Riemannian optimization and interpolating paths ‣ 4 Convergence and the Riemannian toolkit ‣ Riemannian Metric Matchingfor Scalable Geometric Modeling of Distributions" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.​ 2</span></a>.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We select evaluation hyper-parameters via grid search on a held-out validation set, independently for each training-set size.
For metric matching, the only tuned hyper-parameter is the conditioning bandwidth <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>; we evaluate <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}=2^{-k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}=2^{-k}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=-9,-8,\ldots,4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=-9,-8,\ldots,4</annotation></semantics></math> and report test performance using the value that minimizes the validation error.
For the <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-NN graph baseline, we tune both the number of neighbors and the bandwidth, searching over <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=2^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=2^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=3,4\ldots,11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=3,4\ldots,11</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}=2^{-k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}=2^{-k}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=-9,-8,\ldots,4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=-9,-8,\ldots,4</annotation></semantics></math>, and again report test performance for the configuration achieving the lowest validation error.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.4 </span>MNIST experiments</h3>

<section id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">UNet backbone.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use a standard timestep-conditioned UNet backbone with residual blocks and attention from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dhariwal and Nichol, 2021</a>)</cite>. After the final UNet layer, the network outputs a tensor of shape <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[B,K,W,H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[B,K,W,H]</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> is the batch size, <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> are spatial dimensions, and <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of output channels. We then reshape this output to <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[B,K,WH]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[B,K,WH]</annotation></semantics></math> (or equivalently flatten the spatial dimensions) and interpret the channel dimension as a collection of <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> per-pixel feature maps. In our metric-matching parameterization, these <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> channels represent the entries of a low-rank factor: we set <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=Cr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=Cr</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is the input channels (so ambient dimension <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=CWH" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=CWH</annotation></semantics></math>) and reshape the flattened output into a matrix <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{\theta}(x)\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\theta}(x)\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> (per input), where <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is the ambient dimension of the data and <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> is the chosen rank. We then form the predicted (co)metric as the low-rank PSD matrix</p>
<table id="A5.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\Gamma}_{\theta}(x)\;=\;U_{\theta}(x)\,U_{\theta}(x)^{\top}\;\in\;\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\Gamma}_{\theta}(x)\;=\;U_{\theta}(x)\,U_{\theta}(x)^{\top}\;\in\;\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Finally, we optionally add a learned output bias at the UNet head: after the last convolution and before reshaping into <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{\theta}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\theta}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, we add a trainable vector <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in\mathbb{R}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in\mathbb{R}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> to the <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> output channels and broadcast it across spatial dimensions, followed by the reshaping described above.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MNIST configuration.</span>
For MNIST we use <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="28\times 28" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>28</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>28</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">28\times 28</annotation></semantics></math> inputs with <span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">model_channels<math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=64</annotation></semantics></math></span>, <span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">num_res_blocks<math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=2</annotation></semantics></math></span>,
<span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">channel_mult<math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,2,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,2,2)</annotation></semantics></math></span>, and enable attention at downsampling factor <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7\times 7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7\times 7</annotation></semantics></math> feature maps).
We additionally include a learnable output bias term which we initialize a centered normal distribution with <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1e-3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1e-3</annotation></semantics></math> variance, as it empirically improves optimization for early stages of training. We use an output rank of <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=100</annotation></semantics></math> for the low rank parameterization, and use low rank training.
We use Adam optimizer with learning rate <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}=0.999" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.999</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}=0.999</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=10^{-8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=10^{-8}</annotation></semantics></math>, and no weight decay.
Training is run for up to <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1500" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1500</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1500</annotation></semantics></math> epochs with batch size <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>128</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">128</annotation></semantics></math>. We apply gradient clipping with global <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-norm threshold <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Each training step samples a noise/scale parameter <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[h_{\min},h_{\max}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[h_{\min},h_{\max}]</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\min}=10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\min}=10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\max}=25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\max}=25</annotation></semantics></math> using a uniform sampling scheme.
We trained using gaussian augmentation with <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math> standard deviation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Inference parameters.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use a bandwidth of <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}=7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}=7</annotation></semantics></math> as conditioning bandwidth in order to generate <a href="#S5.F3.sf1" title="Figure 3(a) ‣ Figure 3 ‣ 5.1 Synthetic setting: scalability and accuracy ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Riemannian Metric Matchingfor Scalable Geometric Modeling of Distributions" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3(a)</span></a>, <a href="#S5.F3.sf2" title="Figure 3(b) ‣ Figure 3 ‣ 5.1 Synthetic setting: scalability and accuracy ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Riemannian Metric Matchingfor Scalable Geometric Modeling of Distributions" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3(b)</span></a> and <a href="#S5.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ 5.3 Interpolation along the data manifold ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Riemannian Metric Matchingfor Scalable Geometric Modeling of Distributions" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.​ 5</span></a>. For the Riemannian optimization experiment we Riemannian gradient descent with constant learning rate <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.01</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{13}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>13</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{13}</annotation></semantics></math> steps. Additionally, we add a slight isotropic component to the metric replacing <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma^{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma^{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\delta)\Gamma^{\theta}+\delta{\mathbf{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\delta)\Gamma^{\theta}+\delta{\mathbf{I}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math> in order to allow for small movement in all direction, as it improved convergence of the algorithm.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CelebA configuration.</span> For CelebA we use <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64\times 64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64\times 64</annotation></semantics></math> RGB inputs with <span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">model_channels<math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=64</annotation></semantics></math></span>, <span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">num_res_blocks<math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=3</annotation></semantics></math></span>, <span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">channel_mult<math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,2,2,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,2,2,2)</annotation></semantics></math></span>, and enable attention at downsampling factors <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math>. We include a learnable output bias term and use an output rank of <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=128</annotation></semantics></math> for the low-rank parameterization and use low rank training together with the mean-centered loss. Each training step samples a noise/scale parameter <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[h_{\min},h_{\max}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[h_{\min},h_{\max}]</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\min}=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\min}=1.0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\max}=5.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\max}=5.0</annotation></semantics></math> using a uniform sampling scheme. We use the AdamW optimizer with learning rate <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}=0.999" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.999</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}=0.999</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=10^{-8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=10^{-8}</annotation></semantics></math>, with no weight decay. Training is run for up to <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="200" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>200</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">200</annotation></semantics></math> epochs with batch size <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>256</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256</annotation></semantics></math>. We apply gradient clipping with threshold <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For the CelebA posterior mean model used for mean-centered Riemannian metric matching, we use <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64\times 64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64\times 64</annotation></semantics></math> RGB inputs with <span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">model_channels<math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=128</annotation></semantics></math></span>, <span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">num_res_blocks<math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=3</annotation></semantics></math></span>, <span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">channel_mult<math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,2,2,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,2,2,2)</annotation></semantics></math></span>, and enable attention at downsampling factors <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math>. Each training step samples a noise/scale parameter <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[h_{\min},h_{\max}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[h_{\min},h_{\max}]</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\min}=0.002" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.002</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\min}=0.002</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\max}=20.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>20.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\max}=20.0</annotation></semantics></math>, using a uniform sampling scheme. We use the Adam optimizer with learning rate <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}=0.999" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.999</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}=0.999</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=10^{-8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=10^{-8}</annotation></semantics></math>, with no weight decay. Training is run for <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math> epochs. We apply gradient clipping with threshold <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CelebA configuration.</span>
For FFHQ, we use <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256\times 256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>256</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256\times 256</annotation></semantics></math> RGB inputs with <span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">model_channels<math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=128</annotation></semantics></math></span>, <span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">num_res_blocks<math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=2</annotation></semantics></math></span>,
<span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">channel_mult<math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,2,2,4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,2,2,4)</annotation></semantics></math></span>, and enable attention at downsampling factors <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math>.
We include a learnable output bias term and use an output rank of <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=256</annotation></semantics></math> for the low-rank parameterization, together with low-rank training and the mean-centered loss.
Each training step samples a noise/scale parameter <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[h_{\min},h_{\max}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[h_{\min},h_{\max}]</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\min}=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\min}=1.0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\max}=5.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\max}=5.0</annotation></semantics></math>, using a uniform sampling scheme.
We use the AdamW optimizer with learning rate <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}=0.999" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.999</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}=0.999</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=10^{-8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=10^{-8}</annotation></semantics></math>, with no weight decay.
Training is run for up to <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="80" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>80</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">80</annotation></semantics></math> epochs with batch size <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>32</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32</annotation></semantics></math> using <span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">bf16-mixed</span> precision.
We apply gradient clipping with threshold <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">For the FFHQ posterior mean model, we use <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256\times 256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>256</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256\times 256</annotation></semantics></math> RGB inputs with <span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">model_channels<math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=128</annotation></semantics></math></span>, <span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">num_res_blocks<math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=2</annotation></semantics></math></span>,
<span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p5.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">channel_mult<math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,2,2,4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,2,2,4)</annotation></semantics></math></span>, and enable attention at downsampling factors <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math>.
Each training step samples a noise/scale parameter <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[h_{\min},h_{\max}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[h_{\min},h_{\max}]</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\min}=0.002" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.002</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\min}=0.002</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\max}=20.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>20.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\max}=20.0</annotation></semantics></math>, using a uniform sampling scheme.
We use the Adam optimizer with learning rate <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}=0.999" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.999</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}=0.999</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=10^{-8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=10^{-8}</annotation></semantics></math>, with no weight decay.
Training is run for <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="200" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>200</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">200</annotation></semantics></math> epochs with <span id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p5.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">bf16-mixed</span> precision.
We apply gradient clipping with threshold <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Additional results</h2>

<figure id="A6.F6" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2606.14334v1/ffhq_eigenvectors.png" id="A6.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/327;" width="476" height="327" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 6</span>: </span><span id="A6.F6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Visualization of the first <math id="A6.F6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.F6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math>th, <math id="A6.F6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math>th, <math id="A6.F6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>128</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">128</annotation></semantics></math>th, and <math id="A6.F6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>256</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256</annotation></semantics></math>th eigenvectors of the CDC matrix learned by metric matching on FFHQ.
The tangent vectors are shown in grayscale for greater clarity.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A6.F7" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A6.F7.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2606.14334v1/cdc_eigs.svg" id="A6.F7.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/355;" width="476" height="355"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F7.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="A6.F7.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Metric matching MLP (best bandwidth <math id="A6.F7.sf1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A6.F7.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2606.14334v1/cdc_top16_eigs.svg" id="A6.F7.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/355;" width="476" height="355"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F7.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><math id="A6.F7.sf2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.F7.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">-NN CDC estimator (best bandwidth <math id="A6.F7.sf2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.F7.sf2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1024</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="A6.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Mean ordered top <math id="A6.F7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math> eigenvalues on the <math id="A6.F7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional sphere (512k samples), for the best-performing tangent space predictor hyperparameters of (left) metric matching and (right) a <math id="A6.F7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>NN-based CDC estimator.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A6.F8" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2606.14334v1/new_mnist_interp.png" id="A6.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/129;" width="476" height="129" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span id="A6.F8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Interpolation on MNIST. We compare linear interpolation (LERP), metric matching, and the Stein score metric on the interpolation problem.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
